          %p
            and where every possible square in the above is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            square (using the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
          %p
            Notice that for instance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_2
            is identified as such by using that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S^2,-]
            preserves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
            and sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 2
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O \to \tau_{\leq 2} B O
            to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi SO
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
